<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Stocks to Watch Today - March 12.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Stocks to Watch Today - March 12.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some Australian stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* David Jones Ltd A$1.74 (+.03)</p>
<p>Upmarket retailer David Jones Ltd reported a 50 percent lower first half net profit of A$22.34 million and said it expects its pre-tax profit for the second half to be below the previous year. This follows Monday's announcement that chief executive officer Chris Tideman had resigned.</p>
<p>* Santos A$4.98 (+.04)</p>
<p>Oil and gas producer due to report full year results for 1996. Analysts forecast a net profit before abnormals in the range of A$154 million to A$189 million.</p>
<p>*Mayne Nickless A$7.53 (-.02)</p>
<p>*Seven Network A$4.31 (+.03)</p>
<p>Australian Financial Review reports talks aimed at settling disputes over Optus Vision between Seven Network and other Optus shareholders could be resolved within 48 hours.</p>
<p>* Davids Ltd A$1.52 (-.02)</p>
<p>Grocery group Davids Ltd reported a lower first half net profit of A$24.15 million on Tuesday.</p>
<p>* Ashton Mining Ltd A$1.98 (-.04)</p>
<p>Diamond miner Ashton posted a full year profit of 23 percent higher year net profit of A$20.57 million on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
